# MotherDuck credentials (copy to .env.motherduck at repo root — gitignored)
# Use env-token auth only; do not pass tokens on the command line in runbooks.
#
# Read/write tokens (staging, promotion, validators):
#   - MOTHERDUCK_TOKEN — personal developer (default priority in get_token())
#   - MD_SA_TOKEN — CI / service account (use prefer_service_account / --sa where supported)
#
# At least one of the two must be set for --md fail-closed scripts, unless tokens live in
# .streamlit/secrets.toml (see motherduck_client.py).

# Personal (typical laptop workflow)
# MOTHERDUCK_TOKEN=md_your_token_here

# Automation / GitHub Actions
# MD_SA_TOKEN=md_service_account_token_here

# Optional catalog override (default from config/motherduck_environments.yml)
# MOTHERDUCK_DATABASE=Thyroid 2026

# Logical env label (dev/qa/prod); all map to the same DB name in this repo — isolation is by schema
# MOTHERDUCK_ENV=prod

# Read-scaling / dashboard read-only (never use for promotion or v2_stage loaders)
# MD_READ_SCALING_TOKEN=md_read_scaling_token_here
